int and $(X,Y,Z)$ are the corresponding Cartesian coordinates of that point, then we have\n\n$$\nX=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,Y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,Z=z.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Z & ={X}^{2}+{Y}^{2} \\\\ Z & =(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}+(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2} \\\\ Z & ={r}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta ) \\\\ Z & ={r}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, for any point $(x,y,z)$ on our surface, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r,\\theta ) & =⟨x,y,z⟩ \\\\  & =⟨Z,2X,Y⟩ \\\\  & =⟨Z,\\,2r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{r}^{2},\\,2r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $r\\in [0,\\infty )$ and $\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).$\n\nTherefore, the third component of $f$ is $r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .$" 13194139533406 17592186045585 true] [17592186179673 1038 #edb/ref 17592186284677 13194139533406 17592186045585 true] [17592186179674 1038 #edb/ref 17592186284678 13194139533406 17592186045585 true] [17592186179733 1038 #edb/ref 17592186284679 13194139533406 17592186045585 true] [17592186179783 1038 #edb/ref 17592186284409 13194139533406 17592186045585 true] [17592186179783 1038 #edb/ref 17592186284411 13194139533406 17592186045585 true] [17592186179783 1038 #edb/ref 17592186284413 13194139533406 17592186045585 true] [17592186179784 1038 #edb/ref 17592186284418 13194139533406 17592186045585 true] [17592186179784 1038 #edb/ref 17592186284419 13194139533406 17592186045585 true] [17592186179784 1038 #edb/ref 17592186284420 13194139533406 17592186045585 true] [17592186179785 1038 #edb/ref 17592186284406 13194139533406 17592186045585 true] [17592186179785 1038 #edb/ref 17592186284407 13194139533406 17592186045585 true] [17592186179785 1038 #edb/ref 17592186284408 13194139533406 17592186045585 true] [17592186179786 1038 #edb/ref 17592186284410 13194139533406 17592186045585 true] [17592